          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "9951156a-22b2-48a3-9c6c-09192928a96f",
              "name": "text",
              "value": "[IT SUPPORT] Source: https://oit.utdallas.edu/netid/ and https://utdallas.libanswers.com/faq/145887  - If you can't get past the NetID login page, contact the OIT Help Desk at (972) 883-2911, or use the OIT NetID Self-Service portal to reset your password (works from a mobile device).  - The NetID Self-Service page lets students reset or update their password to regain account access.   [FINANCIAL AID] Source: https://finaid.utdallas.edu (Home and Deadlines pages) - The 2027-2028 FAFSA is open. Fall 2027 / Spring 2028 priority deadline: January 15, 2027 for state aid recipients, new freshmen, new transfer, and new graduate students; March 15, 2027 for continuing students. - Fall 2026 / Spring 2027 priority deadlines were January 15, 2026 (state aid and new students) and March 15, 2026 (continuing students). - Summer 2027 priority deadline: March 31, 2027. Summer 2028: March 31, 2028. - To meet the priority deadline, submit a valid FAFSA (or TASFA if not eligible for federal aid) with results received by UT Dallas. Submit at least two weeks early. Students must be admitted to or enrolled in a degree-seeking program. - Check the Orion \"To Do List\" / Tasks tile regularly for additional document requests. - After the priority deadline, students can still apply but should submit at least three weeks before the end of the term. Late applicants may miss some aid programs but can still be considered for Federal Pell Grants and Direct Loans. - Aid begins disbursing on or near the first day of classes and won't show on the Bursar bill until disbursed. - Contact: financial-aid@utdallas.edu, 972-883-2941. Hours: Mon-Thu 9 AM-5 PM, Fri 10 AM-5 PM. FAFSA school code: 009741.  [HOUSING] Source: https://housing.utdallas.edu (Home and Housing Offices pages) - University Housing Office: Andromeda Hall, 955 N Loop Rd., phone 972-883-7430, email housing@utdallas.edu. Hours: Mon-Fri 8 a.m.-5 p.m. - University Village Housing Office: 2800 Waterview Pkwy Ste. 200, phone 972-883-7300. - Maintenance requests can be submitted online through the MyHousing portal, or by phone or walk-in. Emergency maintenance must be reported in person or by calling the resident's building office. - Spring-only housing applications open October 1, 2026 in MyHousing. - First-year housing priority deadline: April 1, 2027.   [ADVISING] Source: https://catalog.utdallas.edu (Undergraduate Policies and Minors pages)  - Students must declare a major by the time they become juniors so that advising is handled by advisors in their school. ",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
